second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"When did the Battle of Cancha Rayada take place?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0188-f0048c7c02b8:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 198, \"text\": \"First Battle of Cancha Rayada The first battle of Cancha Rayada, sometimes termed the 'Disaster' or 'Surprise of Cancha Rayada', took place on 29 March, 1814, during the War of Chilean Independence.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0188-f0048c7c02b8:d00\", \"start\": 199, \"end\": 408, \"text\": \"A patriotic force, under the control of Manuel Blanco Encalada, a Chilean naval officer and later vice-admiral, had advanced towards the town of Talca, which was being held by the guerrilla leader Ángel Calvo.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0188-f0048c7c02b8:d00\", \"start\": 409, \"end\": 543, \"text\": \"Calvo was a Chilean landowner, a former patriot who had switched sides to the Royalists during the Siege of Chillan the previous year.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0188-f0048c7c02b8:d00\", \"start\": 544, \"end\": 616, \"text\": \"Manuel Blanco Encalada arrived in Quechereguas, where he received a note\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0188-f0048c7c02b8:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 252, \"text\": \"Second Battle of Cancha Rayada The Second Battle of Cancha Rayada (March 16, 1818), (also known as the Surprise of Cancha Rayada) was fought in Chile between South American patriots and Spanish royalists, during the South American wars of independence.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0188-f0048c7c02b8:d01\", \"start\": 253, \"end\": 339, \"text\": \"The result was a defeat for the rebels, who took their revenge at the Battle of Maipú.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0188-f0048c7c02b8:d01\", \"start\": 340, \"end\": 616, \"text\": \"In March 1818, the royalist forces concentrated and fortified in Talca with around five thousand men under Brigadier Mariano Osorio, while the independentist forces of around seven thousand men formed by the United Army were taking positions at the Cancha Rayada plains, about\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0188-f0048c7c02b8:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 381, \"text\": \"( 24 ) Macedonian Wars ( 336 – 30 BC ) ( 27 ) Punic Wars ( 37 ) Country ( 640 ) Israel ( 18 ) New Zealand ( 61 ) Portugal ( 187 ) Spain ( 440 ) Wales ( 40 ) Gunpowder Warfare ( 487 ) Carlist Wars ( 54 ) Eighty Years War ( 35 ) English Civil War ( 44 ) Italian Wars ( 33 ) Liberal Wars ( 8 ) Liberators ( 111 ) War in the North ( 6 ) 1813 Araure ( 1 ) 1819 Vargas Swamp ( 2 ) War in\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0188-f0048c7c02b8:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0188-f0048c7c02b8:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"First Battle of Cancha Rayada\", \"scope\": \"Date of the battle\", \"claim\": \"The first battle of Cancha Rayada took place on 29 March, 1814.\", \"answer\": \"29 March, 1814\", \"quote\": \"First Battle of Cancha Rayada The first battle of Cancha Rayada, sometimes termed the 'Disaster' or 'Surprise of Cancha Rayada', took place on 29 March, 1814, during the War of Chilean Independence.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0188-f0048c7c02b8:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0188-f0048c7c02b8:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Second Battle of Cancha Rayada\", \"scope\": \"Date of the battle\", \"claim\": \"The Second Battle of Cancha Rayada took place on March 16, 1818.\", \"answer\": \"March 16, 1818\", \"quote\": \"Second Battle of Cancha Rayada The Second Battle of Cancha Rayada (March 16, 1818), (also known as the Surprise of Cancha Rayada) was fought in Chile between South American